<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1773" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alcyŏnēus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-nĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">halc-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		Alcyone, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to Alcyone</i> or <i>alcyon</i> (v. alcedo). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b> Alcyonei dies = alcedonia (q. v.), <i><span class="en">Col. 11,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			Alcyoneum medicamen, or <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alcyŏnēum</span></b> ,
			i, n., or even <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alcyŏnĭum</span></b> . <i>sea-foam</i>, used as a remedy for spots on the
			face: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alcyoneo utuntur ad oculorum cicatrices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					32, 8, 27, § 86</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Cels. 5, 6, 18</span></i>, n. 26.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
